#. type: Title =
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "OpenEMS: evcc"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"evcc is software for PV surplus charging of electric cars. It controls "
"wallboxes itself and needs grid, PV and storage values for this. For OpenEMS "
"(and FENECON FEMS), evcc comes with **two templates** for meters: one via "
"the REST interface, one via Modbus/TCP. With both, evcc can additionally "
"**control the OpenEMS storage to a certain extent**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"There is no connection in the opposite direction (OpenEMS reads or controls "
"evcc) in the OpenEMS code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"The basis is the templates and source code of evcc as well as the OpenEMS "
"source code. Nothing has been tried out here. The page xref:user/third-party/"
"overview.adoc[Third-party systems on OpenEMS] gives a comparison with Home "
"Assistant and openWB."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two templates"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| \n"
"| “OpenEMS / FENECON – REST-API”\n"
"| “OpenEMS / FENECON – Modbus-API”\n"
"\n"
"| Route\n"
"| HTTP to `+/rest/channel/…+`\n"
"| Modbus/TCP\n"
"| Prerequisite in OpenEMS (read only)\n"
"| REST/JSON API read access\n"
"| Modbus/TCP interface read access\n"
"| Prerequisite (controlling the storage)\n"
"| REST/JSON API read/write access\n"
"| Modbus/TCP interface read/write access\n"
"| Login\n"
"| User “x” and password (basic authentication)\n"
"| none\n"
"| Address\n"
"| Host name; without a port the request goes to port 80\n"
"| Host name and port\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"**Note on the port:** The REST template appends `+/rest/…+` directly to the "
"entered host name. Without a port, evcc therefore queries port 80. On "
"OpenEMS, the REST interface is on port 8084 by default; the address must "
"then be entered with `+:8084+`. The template also specifies a default "
"password, which must match your own system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"For FENECON systems, evcc points out that a paid write app is required for "
"storage control."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"In evcc, you create a separate meter with the same template for each use: "
"**grid**, **PV** and **battery**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Which values are read"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-which-values-are-read
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid "Both templates only read total values (`+_sum+`):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Use in evcc\n"
"| Value\n"
"| Channel in OpenEMS\n"
"| Modbus register (default)\n"
"\n"
".2+| Grid\n"
"| Power\n"
"| `+_sum/GridActivePower+`\n"
"| 315\n"
"| Purchase meter reading\n"
"| `+_sum/GridBuyActiveEnergy+`\n"
"| 359\n"
".2+| PV\n"
"| Power\n"
"| `+_sum/ProductionActivePower+`\n"
"| 327\n"
"| Meter reading\n"
"| `+_sum/ProductionActiveEnergy+`\n"
"| 367\n"
".2+| Battery\n"
"| Power\n"
"| `+_sum/EssDischargePower+`\n"
"| 415\n"
"| State of charge\n"
"| `+_sum/EssSoc+`\n"
"| 302\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"evcc queries the values in its control cycle (default 30 seconds); the REST "
"template keeps each value in the cache for 1 second. Each value is a "
"separate request."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid "For the grid, only the purchase is read, not the feed-in."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"**Modbus registers:** The register numbers are defaults. In OpenEMS, the "
"addresses depend on which components are entered in the Modbus interface and "
"in what order; the Modbus app offers its register table as an Excel file. "
"Recalculated from the code: The defaults match if `+_sum+` is entered as the "
"first component and `+ess0+` as the second component in the Modbus "
"interface. The registers for grid, PV and storage power and the state of "
"charge are then in `+_sum+`. The control register 710 only hits “discharge "
"power at most” of `+ess0+` if its table begins with the usual sections, e.g. "
"with the FENECON Home. With storage systems with an additional section for "
"separate three-phase values (e.g. FENECON Pro, Victron), it is located "
"elsewhere. Therefore compare with your own register table before use."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What evcc can control"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-evcc-can-control
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"If the controllable battery is specified in the battery use (REST: component "
"ID, e.g. `+ess0+`; Modbus: switch “controls battery component”), evcc can "
"put the storage into three operating modes. The same control value is always "
"written, the **upper limit of the storage power** "
"(`+SetActivePowerLessOrEquals+`, see xref:user/external-interfaces/rest-"
"control.adoc#sec-setting-a-control-value[Setting a control value]):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| evcc operating mode\n"
"| Written value\n"
"| Effect in OpenEMS\n"
"\n"
"| Normal\n"
"| 0, once\n"
"| see peculiarity below\n"
"| Hold\n"
"| 0, repeated every 30 seconds\n"
"| Storage may **not discharge**; charging from PV surplus remains possible\n"
"| Charge\n"
"| minus maximum charging power, repeated every 30 seconds\n"
"| Storage is charged with at least this power, from the grid if necessary; only if a maximum charging power is entered in evcc\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"**Repetition:** OpenEMS discards a control value that is not renewed within "
"the Api-Timeout (default 60 seconds). evcc therefore repeats it every half "
"timeout period in the Hold and Charge operating modes. The timeout can be "
"set in the template (“watchdog”, default 60 s) and should match the Api-"
"Timeout of the OpenEMS app."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"**When evcc uses the operating modes:** e.g. “Hold” so that the home storage "
"is not discharged into the car during fast charging (setting “lock battery "
"discharge”), or “Charge” with a low dynamic electricity price (grid charging "
"of the home storage). Without such settings, evcc stays on “Normal”."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"**Peculiarity (from the code of evcc and OpenEMS, not tried out):** For "
"“Normal”, the template writes the value 0 once and does not repeat it. In "
"OpenEMS, the value 0 means “do not discharge”. According to the code, when "
"switching back to “Normal”, discharging therefore remains locked until the "
"Api-Timeout expires (up to 60 seconds) before OpenEMS returns to normal "
"control. According to the OpenEMS code, an empty value, on the other hand, "
"cancels the control value immediately."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"**Not covered:** evcc also has the operating modes “Discharge to grid” and "
"“Hold and charge”. The OpenEMS templates have no entry for these."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-limits
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"**Total values only:** Individual meters, inverters or storage systems are "
"not distinguished."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-limits
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"**Control via one value only:** evcc only specifies an upper limit. All "
"OpenEMS limits continue to apply, e.g. emergency reserve, battery limits and "
"other control functions. Charging at the specified power only succeeds if "
"the battery and inverter allow it (see xref:user/systems/fenecon-home-"
"battery.adoc[FENECON Home battery])."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-limits
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"**Interaction with control functions in OpenEMS:** A time-of-use tariff or "
"grid-optimized charge in OpenEMS work independently of evcc. If evcc "
"specifies “Charge” and OpenEMS something else at the same time, the stricter "
"limit applies in each case. It is best if only one of the two systems "
"controls the storage."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-limits
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"**No memory wear:** Control values are only held in RAM in OpenEMS; frequent "
"writing is harmless (unlike with settings, see xref:user/external-interfaces/"
"websocket.adoc#sec-note-do-not-write-the-configuration-frequently[Note])."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-limits
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"**Unencrypted:** REST with basic authentication in plain text; Modbus/TCP "
"with no login at all. Do not expose ports to the internet."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-limits
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"**Modbus without login:** Anyone who activates the Modbus write app allows "
"every device on the network to control the storage."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid "**REST or Modbus?**"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"REST is easier to set up because the channels are addressed by name. Modbus "
"does not need a login, but the register numbers must match your own system."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"**Why does the storage not discharge again immediately after car charging "
"ends?**"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"See peculiarity above: the last “do not discharge” specification can still "
"apply for up to 60 seconds."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid "**evcc reports no values, error 401 or connection refused.**"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/evcc.adoc
msgid ""
"Check the password (401) and the port: with OpenEMS, usually append "
"`+:8084+` to the address."
msgstr ""
